1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,435
AI has never read a

2
00:00:01,303 --> 00:00:02,519
single word you typed.

3
00:00:02,777 --> 00:00:03,365
Not one.

4
00:00:03,618 --> 00:00:04,964
It only sees numbers .

5
00:00:05,209 --> 00:00:06,773
So what actually happens when

6
00:00:06,649 --> 00:00:07,678
you hit Enter ?

7
00:00:07,922 --> 00:00:09,621
Learn AI engineering, day one.

8
00:00:09,874 --> 00:00:11,168
Let's follow one question.

9
00:00:11,436 --> 00:00:12,937
What's the capital of France?

10
00:00:13,199 --> 00:00:13,815
Step one.

11
00:00:14,068 --> 00:00:14,991
It gets chopped

12
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:15,731
into tokens .

13
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:17,191
Small pieces of words.

14
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,067
Step two.

15
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,280
Every token gets

16
00:00:19,156 --> 00:00:19,839
an ID .

17
00:00:20,083 --> 00:00:21,193
Its row number in

18
00:00:21,063 --> 00:00:22,322
the model's vocabulary .

19
00:00:22,566 --> 00:00:23,728
GPT-2 had 50,257 rows.

20
00:00:23,984 --> 00:00:24,652
Step three.

21
00:00:24,911 --> 00:00:26,303
Every ID becomes a long

22
00:00:26,179 --> 00:00:27,265
list of numbers .

23
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:28,786
768 of them in GPT-2.

24
00:00:29,042 --> 00:00:30,120
That list is the

25
00:00:29,993 --> 00:00:30,935
token's meaning .

26
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:32,600
And here's the smart part.

27
00:00:32,856 --> 00:00:34,312
Every token looks back at

28
00:00:34,182 --> 00:00:35,378
the tokens before it.

29
00:00:35,628 --> 00:00:36,783
So the model learns

30
00:00:36,665 --> 00:00:37,936
that capital and France

31
00:00:37,818 --> 00:00:38,789
belong together .

32
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:40,321
That's called attention .

33
00:00:40,566 --> 00:00:41,439
It comes from

34
00:00:41,315 --> 00:00:42,953
one Google paper, from 2017.

35
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:43,852
Step four.

36
00:00:44,108 --> 00:00:45,353
The model scores every

37
00:00:45,231 --> 00:00:46,491
token in its vocabulary.

38
00:00:46,764 --> 00:00:47,435
Paris wins.

39
00:00:47,691 --> 00:00:48,562
It adds Paris

40
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:49,285
to your text.

41
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:50,417
Then runs the

42
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:51,275
whole thing again.

43
00:00:51,534 --> 00:00:52,779
For every single token.

44
00:00:53,038 --> 00:00:54,551
That's why answers stream in.

45
00:00:54,801 --> 00:00:55,700
One more trick.

46
00:00:55,959 --> 00:00:57,178
It doesn't always pick

47
00:00:57,054 --> 00:00:57,924
the top score.

48
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,863
A setting called temperature adds

49
00:00:59,739 --> 00:01:00,940
a little randomness .

50
00:01:01,185 --> 00:01:02,680
That's why the same question

51
00:01:02,568 --> 00:01:03,839
gets a different answer.

52
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:04,887
So AI isn't

53
00:01:04,763 --> 00:01:05,815
looking anything up.

54
00:01:06,065 --> 00:01:07,627
It's predicting the next piece.

55
00:01:07,886 --> 00:01:09,063
Really, really well.

